00:00:01.599 --> 00:00:03.750 align:start position:0%
 
the realm  do you know what the realm is  it's the thousand blades of aegon's  enemies  a story we agreed to tell each other  over  and over till we forget that it's a lie  what's up ladies and gentlemen welcome  back for another house of the dragon  update video in this video i want to  show you some of the new information  that was revealed about house of the  dragon during a recent interview with  one of the showrunners miguel sapochnick  now for those of you who might not know  miguel sapochnick is famously known for  directing some of game of thrones  greatest episodes like hardhome battle  of the bastards and the winds of winter  after game of thrones ended hbo brought  him on to be one of house of the dragon  showrunners alongside one of its  co-creators ryan condol during this  interview miguel was asked about how  house of the dragon will be different  from game of thrones let me show you  what he said  i think we were very respectful of what  the original show is said saparchnick  who directs multiple episodes of house  of the dragon and also serves as  showrunner alongside the series  co-creator ryan condell it wasn't broken  so we're not trying to reinvent the  wheel house of the dragon has its own  tone that will evolve and emerge over  the course of the show but first it's  very important for us to pay respects  and homage to the original series which  was groundbreaking we are standing on  the shoulders of that show and we're  only here because of that show so the  most important thing for us to do is to  respect that show as much as possible  and try to compliment it rather than  reinvent it and i was involved in making  the original show so i feel like that's  been useful like i'm not arriving going  let's do everything different that said  we can say well when we did thrones we  did it this way he added if you start  every sentence with that you've lost  this is something else and it should be  something else it's a different crew  different people different tone  hopefully it will be seen as something  else but it will have to earn that it  won't happen overnight hopefully fans  will enjoy this for the thing that it is  we'll be lucky if we ever come close to  what the original show was so we're  putting our heads down and getting on  with it and hoping that we come up with  something that is worthy of having a  game of thrones title it's a lot of work  sapochnick said it's a pretty  interesting shift i'm producing other  directors and getting involved in a lot  of the minutia i feel vaguely elated on  my directing days because i don't have  to think about anything other than  directing i've also learned as i've  learned on finch that it's becoming more  and more important to me as i'm getting  older to work with people that i like  alright now i want to show you what some  of the old game of thrones actors had to  say about house of the dragon nikolai  callster waldow also known as jamie  lannister also gave some of his thoughts  about house of the dragon during one of  his recent interviews he said i saw the  teaser trailer that they came out with  and i was intrigued i thought it was fun  to see matt smith in that world and in  that beautiful white wig and listen i'm  curious as everyone but it is a  different show it's its own show i just  hope it's great i hope the success of  game of thrones won't get in the way for  people when they experience this new  show for us it took a while for people  to get into game of thrones i remember  the first season people were saying  there are too many characters i don't  know what's happening i don't think they  have the luxury we had they have to  start with where we were in like season  4 or 5 because that's what they will be  compared to but i really hope that it's  a massive hit for them  kit harrington also known as jon snow  gave some of his thoughts about house of  the dragon as well he said it's being  written and produced and run by a very  good friend of mine miguel sapochnick  who directed me in the original thrones  he said it might be painful to watch you  know i think there's so much tied up in  that that i might find it hard but i  would like to watch it and support him  and support his work and i wish them the  best with that  so as you can see none of this is really  groundbreaking news but i did still find  it to be interesting nonetheless i  always like hearing from some of my  favorite characters from game of thrones  it was also nice to finally hear miguel  sapochnick say a few things about  working on house of the dragon one of  the most exciting things about this new  show is learning that he will definitely  be directing some of the episodes in the  first season this has me very happy  because as i said before miguel has  directed some of game of thrones  greatest episodes knowing that he will  do some of the heavy lifting in the  first season of this new show only sets  them up for success even more he wasn't  directing any episodes on game of  thrones until season 5 but now he will  be hands-on with house of the dragon  from the very beginning which i think is  great now there have also been a lot of  new set photos that i have seen online  let me know if you would like me to make  a video about those they may reveal some  more information about some of the  scenes we will see in this first season  as always i want to thank everyone for  watching this video i hope you all have  a great day i will see you again very  soon  bye  [Music]  [Music]  you

